1
00:00:00,260 --> 00:00:36,510
 This man who has been thrown into jail for not paying his debts, his name is Francisco Pizarro, and he has an interesting story to tell.

2
00:00:36,590 --> 00:00:45,190
 They say he was the son of a Spanish officer and a lady of easy virtue, and then worthy of any good novel, as a newborn baby, he was found on the church steps.

3
00:00:45,730 --> 00:00:49,550
 We know with certainty he was a pig swiller, a farmhand, and a soldier.

4
00:00:50,130 --> 00:00:53,210
 One day, he would leave to conquer the lands of his dreams.

5
00:00:53,650 --> 00:00:56,290
 He would serve many captains, including Ponce de Leon,

6
00:00:56,290 --> 00:00:59,790
 and once, when he was in great danger, Balboa himself saved him.

7
00:01:00,160 --> 00:01:04,250
 But nevertheless, he betrayed Balboa, offering him up to the executioner,

8
00:01:04,530 --> 00:01:06,490
 who went ordered to do so by the governor.

9
00:01:09,050 --> 00:01:12,840
 One day, it was in Panama, a stranger, Pascal Andragoya,

10
00:01:12,960 --> 00:01:17,330
 who had returned from the south, told him a story that was to shape Pizarro's destiny.

11
00:01:17,350 --> 00:01:20,190
 Over hundreds of leagues stands an empire fabulously rich,

12
00:01:20,350 --> 00:01:23,630
 And all the Indians are friendly, covered with gold and jewels.

13
00:01:23,890 --> 00:01:25,750
 Houses covered with gold. Gold!

14
00:01:28,370 --> 00:01:34,010
 And I will supply funds for your expedition.

15
00:01:34,170 --> 00:01:35,890
 20,000 pesos and gold bars.

16
00:01:36,810 --> 00:01:37,390
 Uh-huh.

17
00:01:38,290 --> 00:01:46,410
 You will swear a pact, a solemn pact.

18
00:01:46,630 --> 00:01:48,930
 Pizarro, Amalgoro, you shall swear on the Holy Bible.

19
00:01:50,720 --> 00:02:20,700
 We sailed with no further ado.

20
00:02:21,770 --> 00:02:25,160
 As for their return, it was somewhat less auspicious.

21
00:02:27,090 --> 00:02:41,310
 You mustn't lose all hope.

22
00:02:41,900 --> 00:02:45,260
 I shall state our case personally when we see Governor Pedrarias.

23
00:02:45,700 --> 00:02:48,160
 If that fool Pizarro wants to depart, then let him.

24
00:02:48,660 --> 00:02:52,560
 In six months, whether in Peru or not, I order you to be back in Panama.

25
00:02:53,990 --> 00:02:54,470
 Obit.

26
00:03:47,590 --> 00:04:07,780
 Petition ran a...

27
00:04:07,780 --> 00:04:12,730
 Is Almagro going to show up with his troops?

28
00:04:13,160 --> 00:04:15,200
 Are we going to spend the rest of our days here?

29
00:04:19,650 --> 00:04:25,640
 Six months have gone by.

30
00:04:25,800 --> 00:04:29,930
 Following the governor's orders, we return to Panama, and at once...

31
00:04:29,930 --> 00:04:32,770
 I must be alone here, I will remain.

32
00:04:36,870 --> 00:04:39,510
 To this line, poverty and misery await you.

33
00:04:39,510 --> 00:04:42,790
 To the south, there is danger, famine.

34
00:04:43,430 --> 00:04:45,810
 We might be killed, but we might be rich.

35
00:04:46,130 --> 00:04:46,790
 Riches await.

36
00:04:47,130 --> 00:04:51,350
 Every one of us goes with me to conquer gold.

37
00:04:51,390 --> 00:05:04,530
 A dozen men crossed the line.

38
00:05:10,420 --> 00:05:14,420
 Seven months later, with Almagro's reinforcements, which finally arrived,

39
00:05:14,540 --> 00:05:16,340
 Bizarro takes to the sea again.

40
00:05:16,680 --> 00:05:20,500
 After sailing for 20 days, here he is in sight of the city of Chumbaz.

41
00:05:23,370 --> 00:05:30,300
 Take some men in reconnoiter of the city for us.

42
00:05:30,590 --> 00:05:32,520
 Take a good look, then report back to me.

43
00:05:32,820 --> 00:05:34,070
 Aye, aye, sir.

44
00:05:36,020 --> 00:05:38,860
 Tell me, what's the city like?

45
00:05:39,270 --> 00:05:43,300
 Their princess Capilana served us on golden plates, and gold goblets as well.

46
00:05:43,560 --> 00:05:44,890
 Her robes were of gold.

47
00:05:44,890 --> 00:05:46,590
 Yes, go on.

48
00:05:47,000 --> 00:05:50,730
 Well, they're all nice, but the women are extraordinarily beautiful.

49
00:05:50,850 --> 00:05:53,410
 If you'll allow, Captain, I'll stay here and convert the natives.

50
00:05:53,650 --> 00:05:54,070
 Wait.

51
00:05:55,780 --> 00:05:59,190
 Send Pedro de Cogna ashore to gather more information for me.

52
00:05:59,600 --> 00:06:00,140
 Aye, aye, sir.

53
00:06:00,590 --> 00:06:03,190
 All the walls of their temples are covered with gold.

54
00:06:03,490 --> 00:06:05,550
 They're massive statues of animals in gold.

55
00:06:05,920 --> 00:06:07,640
 Statues in gold, animals in gold.

56
00:06:07,720 --> 00:06:08,500
 Don't stop there.

57
00:06:08,580 --> 00:06:10,180
 You won't believe the animals I saw.

58
00:06:10,180 --> 00:06:11,400
 They were strange.

59
00:06:12,250 --> 00:06:12,950
 Pitting cows.

60
00:06:14,030 --> 00:06:15,670
 Yes, but their fortress is strong.

61
00:06:16,220 --> 00:06:19,380
 Yes, three massive concentric walls, all strongly guarded.

62
00:06:19,620 --> 00:06:20,140
 Impenetrable.

63
00:06:20,790 --> 00:06:23,770
 I will beat them! I will beat them!

64
00:06:25,390 --> 00:06:28,730
 Get up, Captain. You'll want it, and by who, you'll never guess.

65
00:06:29,160 --> 00:06:30,570
 Clean yourself up.

66
00:06:31,090 --> 00:06:35,850
 In the city of Tumbes, there's gold and riches beyond dreams, Your Majesty.

67
00:06:37,790 --> 00:06:41,160
 Toledo. Charles V, his power at its highest.

68
00:06:41,320 --> 00:06:43,400
 Cortez brings back three tons of gold every year.

69
00:06:43,640 --> 00:06:45,180
 Francois I, he beat at Pavia.

70
00:06:46,380 --> 00:06:49,230
 His troops have just sacked Rome.

71
00:06:49,230 --> 00:06:53,290
 And the Pope is waiting to crown him emperor.

72
00:06:53,610 --> 00:06:55,550
 Suddenly, Pizarro's story interests him.

73
00:06:56,220 --> 00:07:00,040
 There are a great many souls to convert to our religion, Your Majesty.

74
00:07:00,880 --> 00:07:05,650
 The governor of Panama failed to grasp the importance of this land,

75
00:07:06,630 --> 00:07:09,530
 so I came to see you, Your Majesty.

76
00:07:10,880 --> 00:07:12,920
 You have done well, Pizarro, quite well.

77
00:07:13,000 --> 00:07:14,850
 Now tell me, what was your journey like?

78
00:07:16,340 --> 00:07:18,060
 Easy, a pleasure cruise.

79
00:07:18,460 --> 00:07:19,780
 I assure you, Your Majesty.

80
00:07:23,760 --> 00:07:29,620
 Well, Pizarro, go back and conquer it for us.

81
00:07:29,680 --> 00:07:32,350
 At your orders, Majesty, I will leave as soon as I can.

82
00:07:32,350 --> 00:07:34,680
 You shall have 200 soldiers and 30 horsemen.

83
00:07:35,920 --> 00:07:37,700
 Almagro will become governor of Tumbez,

84
00:07:37,960 --> 00:07:40,130
 And Padre de Lugue shall be the bishop.

85
00:07:41,590 --> 00:07:44,830
 As for you, I appoint you Captain Governor of Peru,

86
00:07:46,500 --> 00:07:48,800
 Knight of Santiago and the Marquis.

87
00:07:54,800 --> 00:07:59,820
 Far away in Peru.

88
00:08:00,610 --> 00:08:02,360
 It's good to get home again.

89
00:08:02,500 --> 00:08:04,400
 Yes, especially after losing a war.

90
00:08:04,540 --> 00:08:07,020
 Our Lord Waskin is being held prisoner at Cusco.

91
00:08:07,720 --> 00:08:10,050
 I wonder what's going to happen now.

92
00:08:10,700 --> 00:08:11,920
 Who knows?

93
00:08:12,300 --> 00:08:14,100
 Well, we had fun all the same, didn't we?

94
00:08:14,100 --> 00:08:16,900
 I wonder what our planting grounds look like.

95
00:08:17,140 --> 00:08:18,100
 We've been gone so long.

96
00:08:34,170 --> 00:08:35,650
 They'll need lots of work.

97
00:08:39,650 --> 00:08:43,360
 How's daddy's big boy?

98
00:09:17,730 --> 00:09:47,090
 call you Pedriti, and will carefully keep some of your hair and your nails, attention of yourself.

99
00:09:47,450 --> 00:09:49,830
 No evil spirit can use them against you.

100
00:09:53,000 --> 00:10:00,400
 This beautiful, when you're 12 years old, maybe you will be chosen to pay homage to Wallaboo,

101
00:10:00,480 --> 00:10:03,200
 the god of fertility, and be thrown into the abyss.

102
00:10:03,200 --> 00:10:05,640
 It's an honor performed in a beautiful ceremony.

103
00:10:05,800 --> 00:10:08,800
 You might go as one of the 5,000 concubines of the Inca.

104
00:10:10,370 --> 00:10:11,660
 Could be a sun virgin.

105
00:10:17,410 --> 00:10:24,610
 A bit later, when you two are married, you'll get a house, and I will tie a knot in my kipu.

106
00:10:25,780 --> 00:10:33,160
 Yes, you'll have a planting field, and that's another knot, and you'll have two llamas as well, two knots, and about here I'll keep for your children.

107
00:10:34,590 --> 00:10:36,370
 Not for each one.

108
00:10:36,530 --> 00:10:40,310
 All those knots are complicated. I mean, there are so many. Ever get mixed up?

109
00:10:40,830 --> 00:10:43,950
 Well, I'd better not. No, it's my head otherwise.

110
00:10:44,670 --> 00:10:46,490
 The order has to prevail to govern well.

111
00:10:48,190 --> 00:10:52,040
 When I think of all the delicious meat that's in there...

112
00:10:52,040 --> 00:10:56,860
 The Incas are stocking up for the lean years ahead, and I think it's a wise thing to do.

113
00:10:59,090 --> 00:11:12,500
 This? Careful now, don't load him with more than 30 kilograms.

114
00:11:12,500 --> 00:11:14,850
 Uh...

115
00:11:14,850 --> 00:11:19,170
 *laughter*

116
00:11:19,170 --> 00:11:46,010
 Turn thing up alright.

117
00:11:46,010 --> 00:11:48,730
 Our message service has never been so busy.

118
00:11:48,730 --> 00:11:56,320
 And what is up is that Pizarro has just landed at Tumbez, that the Inca communication system is the finest anywhere in the world.

119
00:11:56,320 --> 00:12:09,020
 Talor...

120
00:12:09,020 --> 00:12:10,460
 *sounds of silence*

121
00:12:10,460 --> 00:12:15,360
 Was I supposed to know what's going on in this place? An explanation!

122
00:12:15,360 --> 00:12:19,970
 *sounds of silence*

123
00:12:19,970 --> 00:12:22,620
 Hey, Filipilo, what's going on?

124
00:12:22,620 --> 00:12:30,750
 In a nutshell, the great Inca Lord Huayna Capac died right after you passed through last time and his sons waged war in alterations.

125
00:12:30,750 --> 00:12:32,090
 Go on. Well?

126
00:12:32,090 --> 00:12:39,260
 Then, one of the two brothers, Huascar, lost and is a prisoner. Atahualpa, the winner, massacred the lot, even his sister Koenig. Zip!

127
00:12:39,260 --> 00:12:41,730
 It's pretty bloody, huh?

128
00:12:41,730 --> 00:12:48,190
 Anyway, in your armor to them, you look like, in fact, you are Viracocha, the thunder god.

129
00:12:48,190 --> 00:13:25,250
 Hey, versions to do.

130
00:13:25,250 --> 00:13:31,330
 Now listen to me, Diego. Once we've set things up around here, you'll go south to chill you.

131
00:13:31,330 --> 00:13:36,000
 Believe me, there's gold in the streets down there in Chile, and it's all yours.

132
00:13:37,930 --> 00:13:43,000
 My blood brothers, Hernando, Juan, Gonzales, Padre Valverde de Soto, follow me.

133
00:13:43,330 --> 00:13:44,510
 We go forward.

134
00:14:00,380 --> 00:14:17,220
 Marca isn't far now.

135
00:14:17,990 --> 00:14:20,450
 Atahualpa is waiting for us. You'll see him tomorrow.

136
00:14:20,990 --> 00:14:41,520
 We'll make him c-

137
00:14:41,520 --> 00:15:09,790
 The Lord Atahualpa is his pleasure to-

138
00:15:09,790 --> 00:15:23,190
 My storeroom.

139
00:15:23,400 --> 00:15:24,000
 Tell me why.

140
00:15:25,920 --> 00:15:28,030
 We're responsible for building them.

141
00:15:28,630 --> 00:15:29,750
 The labor of my people.

142
00:15:29,850 --> 00:15:31,070
 Yes, give back the goods.

143
00:15:34,430 --> 00:15:34,910
 Them away.

144
00:15:36,140 --> 00:15:37,730
 What will you do to those men?

145
00:15:39,900 --> 00:15:44,600
 Shall kill them. They showed no dignity in their rank.

146
00:15:44,600 --> 00:15:50,280
 Go tell your master we will meet him tomorrow in this place.

147
00:15:55,010 --> 00:16:00,950
 There are 40,000 of them, and we are only 170.

148
00:16:01,210 --> 00:16:01,850
 What can we do?

149
00:16:02,090 --> 00:16:02,500
 Pray.

150
00:16:03,200 --> 00:16:27,200
 Come, Hernando, Juan, Gonzales, Lesotho, Rocandia, Belacazar, Padre.

151
00:16:27,870 --> 00:16:30,810
 This is what we'll do.

152
00:16:33,020 --> 00:16:36,640
 It looks like we're surrounded.

153
00:16:44,060 --> 00:16:49,590
 Hey, look at that!

154
00:17:04,280 --> 00:17:27,420
 Reigns over the universe.

155
00:17:28,030 --> 00:17:33,130
 Its vicar, our Holy Father, the Pope, has given the King of Spain dominion over these lands,

156
00:17:33,130 --> 00:17:37,630
 and you must be a friend to our sovereign King of Spain and submit to his will.

157
00:17:37,810 --> 00:17:42,120
 Is it not astonishing that your Pope can give away what is not his?

158
00:17:42,120 --> 00:17:44,450
 Where is the proof of what you say?

159
00:17:44,450 --> 00:17:55,930
 Say all this means nothing.

160
00:17:55,930 --> 00:18:12,890
 Until...

161
00:18:12,890 --> 00:18:36,270
 A thousand Incas killed on the spot and not one Spaniard wounded.

162
00:18:36,270 --> 00:18:40,270
 One of those strange quirks of history with a handful of soldiers, Pizarro,

163
00:18:40,270 --> 00:18:43,840
 put an end to the powerful empire of the Incas.

164
00:18:43,840 --> 00:18:49,500
 There would still be incidents, but the die was cast.

165
00:18:49,500 --> 00:18:54,190
 This is a nice article.

166
00:18:54,190 --> 00:19:12,990
 The Aztec prisoners, Filippillo, lost his heart to a very beautiful slave.

167
00:19:12,990 --> 00:19:16,960
 And so he concocted a plan to do away with Atahualp.

168
00:19:16,960 --> 00:19:20,960
 Believe us, I heard it all!

169
00:19:20,960 --> 00:19:28,550
 Brother Huascar killed, and you're plotting against me now.

170
00:19:28,550 --> 00:19:30,100
 I am not plotting.

171
00:19:30,100 --> 00:19:31,290
 A stupid idea.

172
00:19:31,290 --> 00:19:34,800
 With the hoard of gold I have, how much to buy my freedom?

173
00:19:34,800 --> 00:19:37,530
 Perhaps up to my hand would that buy it?

174
00:19:37,530 --> 00:19:46,400
 Here, then.

175
00:19:46,400 --> 00:20:03,950
 Borship of idols, adultery, incest, murder of brothers, and rebellion.

176
00:20:03,950 --> 00:20:08,830
 The sentence is death by Garrett, and then burnt up!

177
00:20:10,700 --> 00:20:15,730
 Then I will never see my ancestors again.

178
00:20:15,890 --> 00:20:18,310
 Why will you not convert to our holy faith?

179
00:20:18,590 --> 00:20:20,910
 Then will you still burn my body?

180
00:20:21,490 --> 00:20:21,880
 No.

181
00:20:22,120 --> 00:20:23,930
 Then I'll be happy to do what you say.

182
00:20:24,090 --> 00:20:26,110
 It was a strange conversion, all right.

183
00:20:27,110 --> 00:20:29,910
 Judgment, verdict, baptism, execution, all in one day.

184
00:20:30,680 --> 00:20:32,260
 Haste with no good reason.

185
00:20:32,750 --> 00:20:37,330
 I've combed the land and found no sign of uprising or rebellion, as he describes.

186
00:20:40,290 --> 00:20:42,900
 You can't kill him.

187
00:20:43,310 --> 00:20:44,950
 You have no right to kill him.

188
00:20:44,950 --> 00:20:49,960
 He was a most noble ruler. He gave you all that gold.

189
00:20:55,370 --> 00:20:59,860
 These marvelous treasures, these superb objects, all melted into bars.

190
00:21:01,270 --> 00:21:03,480
 Your share against mine, right?

191
00:21:11,420 --> 00:21:21,490
 His brother Manco Capac to keep them quiet.

192
00:21:21,760 --> 00:21:23,780
 Almalgo and I will return to the coast.

193
00:21:24,710 --> 00:21:28,300
 I remember, but Hernando, you'll really be in command.

194
00:21:29,810 --> 00:21:32,490
 Manco Capac, we name you Lord Inca.

195
00:21:33,090 --> 00:21:35,420
 We'll take the place of your brother Atahualpa.

196
00:21:36,250 --> 00:21:38,470
 Brother Hernando will be here to help.

197
00:21:38,470 --> 00:21:43,600
 In our regions to the south are many riches, and much gold which you seem so interested in.

198
00:21:43,860 --> 00:21:46,370
 If you wish, my brother Paulo can guide you.

199
00:22:15,130 --> 00:22:33,250
 ...managed to get rid of the greater part of the Spanish troops, and raised 400,000 men for the siege of Cusco.

200
00:22:33,270 --> 00:22:33,370
 Forward!

201
00:22:34,430 --> 00:22:37,320
 Because flies will never beat that crowd!

202
00:22:42,100 --> 00:22:45,420
 Almagro's army returning to attack them, and to take the city.

203
00:22:46,280 --> 00:22:49,860
 Almagro was to lose the fratricidal battle of Las Salinas.

204
00:22:50,910 --> 00:22:51,110
 Aha!

205
00:22:52,230 --> 00:22:54,400
 Been friends, your brother and I.

206
00:22:54,740 --> 00:22:56,830
 Put me in prison for the little time I have left.

207
00:22:56,830 --> 00:22:57,760
 No, I won't!

208
00:22:57,760 --> 00:23:05,660
 Spago was strangled while imprisoned three months later in the city of Lima where Francisco Pizarro lived in a palace.

209
00:23:07,260 --> 00:23:09,020
 Quack!

210
00:23:09,020 --> 00:23:45,040
 Before being taken and degorged himself, in the same year, Padre Valverde would be killed by India.

211
00:23:45,040 --> 00:23:52,990
 Their adventure, in spite of everything, is surely going to remain one of the most extraordinary lived by mere mortals.

